<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hex harness launchd template (spec S5yw25n5y; gui LaunchAgent form 2026-06-05).

  This is a per-user gui LaunchAgent (installed to ~/Library/LaunchAgents), NOT a
  system LaunchDaemon. Reason: per the hex-as-own-harness design the harness runs
  per-task reasoning INSIDE `claude`, and Claude Code auth lives in the macOS
  LOGIN keychain — which a system daemon (no login session) cannot reach. A gui
  LaunchAgent bootstrapped into gui/<uid> runs in the user's Aqua login session
  and inherits its unlocked login keychain.

  NO `SessionCreate`. Empirically verified 2026-06-05 (keychain-launchagent-test):
  a gui agent WITHOUT SessionCreate reads the login keychain (rc=0); WITH it the
  read is BLOCKED (rc=36 errSecAuthFailed). `SessionCreate=true` spawns the job
  into a NEW audit session, DETACHING it from the Aqua session that holds the
  unlocked login keychain (per `man launchd.plist`). So it HURTS keychain access.
  Do not re-add it. (macOS 26: spawn `claude` as a DIRECT program, not `bash ->
  claude`, so the keychain-ACL identity stays clean.)

  Tradeoff vs a daemon: dies on logout. Accepted — FileVault forces a GUI login
  at every boot on this box, so there's effectively always a login session, and
  keychain access (which the harness needs for claude) is worth more than
  surviving an explicit logout.

  `hex harness start` renders this template by substituting:
    HEXBIN_PLACEHOLDER -> $HEX_DIR/.hex/bin/hex
    HEXDIR_PLACEHOLDER -> $HEX_DIR
    PATH_PLACEHOLDER   -> runtime PATH (homebrew prepended)
    LOG_PLACEHOLDER    -> $HEX_DIR/.hex/logs/com.hex.harness.log

  The harness is a single-process drain-aware host for the typed Rust workers
  in `hex::workers::registry()`. The hidden `hex harness serve` entry IS the
  long-running process — launchd invokes it; humans use `start|stop|status`.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.hex.harness</string>
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>HEXBIN_PLACEHOLDER</string>
        <string>harness</string>
        <string>serve</string>
    </array>
    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>HEXDIR_PLACEHOLDER</string>
    <!-- Intentionally NO SessionCreate — it detaches the job from the Aqua login
         session and BLOCKS login-keychain access (verified: rc=36 with it, rc=0
         without). A plain gui/<uid> agent inherits the keychain. -->
    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>HEX_DIR</key>
        <string>HEXDIR_PLACEHOLDER</string>
        <key>III_URL</key>
        <string>ws://127.0.0.1:49134</string>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>PATH_PLACEHOLDER</string>
        <!-- gws (Drive backup) keeps the FILE keyring — it's a separate secret
             from claude's keychain auth and the file backend is robust either
             way. (Switch to the login keychain later if we want full uniformity.) -->
        <key>GOOGLE_WORKSPACE_CLI_KEYRING_BACKEND</key>
        <string>file</string>
    </dict>
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>
    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <dict>
        <key>SuccessfulExit</key>
        <false/>
    </dict>
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>LOG_PLACEHOLDER</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>LOG_PLACEHOLDER</string>
    <key>ProcessType</key>
    <string>Background</string>
</dict>
</plist>
